independent per-view sort state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No filter feature exists in the app\", \"actual\": \"Searched the entire toolbar, table headers, card view, and full page DOM for any filter control (button, icon, or panel). No 'Filter' text, no funnel/filter icon (lucide-filter), and no filter-related data-semtag elements were found anywhere. Only Sort, Search, view toggles, Add Entry, and Fields controls exist. There is no way to define field-specific filter criteria.\", \"evidence\": \"Full-page innerHTML search for the substring 'filter' returned no matches; enumerated all SVG icon classes on the page (database, settings2, search, arrow-up-down, table2, layout-grid, plus, grip-vertical, x, pencil, trash2, check) - none related to filtering.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With no field sort active, dragged entry-1's drag handle onto entry-3 in table view -> order became [entry-2,entry-3,entry-1,entry-4,entry-5,new]. Separately dragged entry-1 onto entry-3 in card view -> same result there. Then dragged entry-4 to top in table view only -> table order became [entry-4,entry-2,entry-3,entry-1,entry-5,new] while card view retained its own order [entry-2,entry-3,entry-1,entry-4,entry-5,new] unchanged after switching, proving independent manual order per view.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No import feature exists in the app\", \"actual\": \"The Fields configuration dialog only contains a note stating 'Configure fields before importing data', but there is no actual import button, file picker, or data-paste control anywhere in the dialog or the rest of the app. A full-page HTML search for 'import' only found this note text, no functional import control. Therefore importing data and validating type-mismatch rejection cannot be performed.\", \"evidence\": \"fields.dialog snapshot contains only field rows, a New-field name