r every entry in both views with matching values.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Field-config type select shows clearly labeled options: Text, Number, Date, Checkbox. Entry form renders type-appropriate native controls: field-1 <input type=text>, field-2 <input type=number>, field-3 <input type=date>, field-4 <button role=checkbox> toggle.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Table view: checked entries show a green check icon (lucide-check, text-success), unchecked show a muted X icon (lucide-x, text-muted-foreground). Card view: checked shows 'Yes', unchecked shows 'No'. Entry form uses a toggle switch control (entry.field-4) with distinct true/false states.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Search matches only raw internal values, not the formatted values shown to users\", \"actual\": \"Searching for the displayed due-date text 'Jan 15' (as shown 'Jan 15, 2026' in both views) returned '0 entries matching', while searching the raw ISO value '2026-01-15' returned '1 entry matching'. Searching the displayed checkbox label 'Yes' (shown in card view) returned '0 entries matching' even though 2 entries are checked/'Yes'.\", \"evidence\": \"statusbar.count values: 'Jan 15' -> '0 entries matching \\\\\\\"Jan 15\\\\\\\"'; '2026-01-15' -> '1 entry matching \\\\\\\"2026-01-15\\\\\\\"'; 'Yes' -> '0 entries matching \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\"'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searching 'landing' filtered to 1 matching entry ('Design new landing page'), statusbar showed '1 entry matching \\\\\\\"landing\\\\\\\"'. Searching uppercase 'LANDING' produced the identical single-match result, confirming case-insensitivity. Clicking clear-search button restored statusbar to '6 entries' with all entries visible again.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\